Priya, Marcus,

Attached is the pilot proposal, built on the Reno data Priya shared. Headline: on those two weeks, our simulator releases work 9 minutes earlier on average per wave and keeps AMRs busy 17% more of the shift.

Two options:

Option A: one site. Reno only, 8 weeks, up to 40 pickers on both shifts. Flat $18,000, credited against year one. Success metric: picks per labor hour vs. the June baseline, measured by Tom's team, not ours.

Option B: three sites. Reno, Columbus and Allentown in parallel, 10 weeks. $45,000. Faster path to a full rollout decision, but three network reviews and three change windows.

My honest recommendation is Option A. It proves the thing that matters with the least disruption, and Columbus and Allentown can follow in weeks rather than months if Reno works.

Either option needs a security review on your side before the agent goes on the floor network. Dana has our standard package ready.

